      "sourceTextSha256": "46d76456aa6926ecd4f0b39c62da95f268388b6c3cd7f1b7672677adbb6c83ae",
      "text": "After breakfast, visit the Argentine side of the falls with an English-speaking guide. Paths and footbridges run above and between the streams, bringing you closer to individual cascades. As you walk through the park, you may see orchids, birds, butterflies, reptiles and other inhabitants of the tropical rainforest.\n\nA highlight is the ecological train ride followed by a walk to the Devil’s Throat viewpoint, overlooking the most powerful cascade in the system. Together with the previous day’s visit, this excursion gives you both a panoramic view of Iguazú and a close look from the walkways within the falls.",
      "provenance": {
